From: PiercingXX <155384428+PiercingXX@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:20:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] TextInput: send enter to a text input created by the focused
 client

InputRelay.focus() sends zwp_text_input_v3.enter only when keyboard
focus changes or an input method appears. A client that creates its
text input while it already has focus never receives enter, so it can
never enable the text input and the input method is never activated.
GTK4 creates its text input on the first frame that shows a text field,
which is often after the window was focused: a field that first appears
on a later page gets no on-screen keyboard until focus leaves the app
and comes back.

On a new text input, send enter if the seat's focused surface belongs
to the same client (labwc does the same in handle_new_text_input).
---
 river/TextInput.zig | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/river/TextInput.zig b/river/TextInput.zig
index 3a73936..56776cd 100644
--- a/river/TextInput.zig
+++ b/river/TextInput.zig
@@ -42,6 +42,18 @@ pub fn create(wlr_text_input: *wlr.TextInputV3) !void {
     wlr_text_input.events.commit.add(&text_input.commit);
     wlr_text_input.events.disable.add(&text_input.disable);
     wlr_text_input.events.destroy.add(&text_input.destroy);
+
+    // A client may create its text input after it already has keyboard
+    // focus (GTK4 does so on the first frame that shows a text field).
+    // InputRelay.focus() only sends enter when focus changes, so send it
+    // here too or the text input can never be enabled.
+    if (seat.relay.input_method != null) {
+        if (seat.focused.surface()) |surface| {
+            if (surface.resource.getClient() == wlr_text_input.resource.getClient()) {
+                wlr_text_input.sendEnter(surface);
+            }
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 fn handleEnable(listener: *wl.Listener(void)) void {
